(defrule prompt-construction -> prompt-construction-role prompt-construction-monolith prompt-construction-pipeline prompt-construction-tiers prompt-construction-modes prompt-construction-variables prompt-construction-providers prompt-construction-caching prompt-construction-fallback)
(defrule prompt-construction-role -> :nucleus prompt-construction-role/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-role/a1 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-role/a2)
(defrule prompt-construction-role/n -> :instruction "指示文が振る舞いの制御で果たす役割を 1 文で書く" :sample "In an LLM-based agent, the system prompt is the primary instrument of behavioral control: it encodes the agent’s identity, capability boundaries, safety constraints, and task conventions.")
(defrule prompt-construction-role/a1 -> :instruction "指示文にしか書けない性質を例示して 1 文で書く" :sample "Every behavioral property that cannot be enforced through code, how the agent reasons, which tools it prefers, how it recovers from errors, is expressed as natural language in the system prompt.")
(defrule prompt-construction-role/a2 -> :instruction "これが初期化の中心の問題であることを 1 文で書く" :sample "Getting this prompt right at startup is therefore not a minor configuration detail; it is the central initialization problem.")
(defrule prompt-construction-monolith -> :nucleus prompt-construction-monolith/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-monolith/a1 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-monolith/a2 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-monolith/a3)
(defrule prompt-construction-monolith/n -> :instruction "全部入りの単一の指示文という素朴な方式を 1 文で書く" :sample "A naive approach loads a single monolithic prompt containing every possible instruction.")
(defrule prompt-construction-monolith/a1 -> :instruction "その方式の一つ目の費用を 1 文で書く" :sample "First, sections that are irrelevant to the current session (such as git workflow rules in a non-repository directory, subagent orchestration guidance when subagents are unused, or task-tracking instructions when the feature is disabled) consume context-window budget without contributing any behavioral value.")
(defrule prompt-construction-monolith/a2 -> :instruction "二つ目の費用を 1 文で書く" :sample "Second, irrelevant instructions dilute the sections that do matter, making the agent’s behavior noisier.")
(defrule prompt-construction-monolith/a3 -> :instruction "対策の方針を 1 文で書く" :sample "The fix is not to trim the prompt by hand, but to make loading context-sensitive from the start.")
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline -> :nucleus prompt-construction-pipeline/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-pipeline/a1 :elaboration-set-member prompt-construction-pipeline/a2)
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline/n -> :instruction "指示文を実行時に組み立てる流れと、節ごとの付随情報を 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev assembles each agent’s system prompt at runtime through the pipeline illustrated in Figure 10.")
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline/a1 -> :instruction "組み立て役が行う段階の数を 1 文で書く" :sample "At initialization the PromptComposer executes four steps:")
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline/a2 -> :instruction "段階を 1 項目ずつ、段階の名前と何をするかで書く" :sample "Filter. Evaluate each section’s predicate against the current environment snapshot. Sections that return False are excluded before any file I/O occurs. For example, main-git-workflow.md is gated on in_git_repo; it is never loaded when the working directory is not a repository. / Sort. Order the surviving sections by ascending priority: lower values appear earlier, placing identity and persona rules before environment-derived context. / Load. Read each markdown file, strip human-readable frontmatter, and resolve ${VAR} placeholders via a centralized name registry that decouples template prose from concrete tool identifiers. / Join. Concatenate loaded sections and append to the core role text and dynamically collected environment block, producing the complete system prompt." :kind bullet)
(defrule prompt-construction-tiers -> :nucleus prompt-construction-tiers/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-tiers/a1)
(defrule prompt-construction-tiers/n -> :instruction "標準の動作モードの指示文が登録する節の層を 1 文で書く" :sample "The default action-mode agent registers modular sections across five functional tiers: Core Identity for persona and non-negotiable constraints, Tool Definitions for tool-use and code-quality guidance needed during execution, Safety & Rules for conditionally loaded policies such as git conventions and task-tracking instructions, Provider-Specific Guidance for LLM-provider-specific behavioral hints, and Dynamic Context for session-specific metadata.")
(defrule prompt-construction-tiers/a1 -> :instruction "考えるモードの指示文が節を減らす理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "The thinking-mode agent registers fewer sections, deliberately omitting tool-use guidance to avoid biasing tool-free reasoning toward premature action.")
(defrule prompt-construction-modes -> :nucleus prompt-construction-modes/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-modes/a1 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-modes/a2 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-modes/a3)
(defrule prompt-construction-modes/n -> :instruction "推論の段階ごとに指示文が違う必要を 1 文で書く" :sample "Different reasoning phases require fundamentally different prompts.")
(defrule prompt-construction-modes/a1 -> :instruction "通常モードの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "Normal (action) mode loads all registered sections across five tiers.")
(defrule prompt-construction-modes/a2 -> :instruction "計画モードの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "Planning mode uses a standalone template optimized for read-only exploration.")
(defrule prompt-construction-modes/a3 -> :instruction "モードの違いを実現する手段を 1 文で書く" :sample "This mode specialization is achieved through a factory function: create_composer(templates_dir, mode=\"system/main\") returns the full action composer, while mode=\"system/thinking\" returns the minimal thinking composer.")
(defrule prompt-construction-variables -> :nucleus prompt-construction-variables/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-variables/a1)
(defrule prompt-construction-variables/n -> :instruction "指示文の雛形が置換される仕組みを 1 文で書く" :sample "Templates use ${VAR} placeholders resolved at render time by a PromptRenderer.")
(defrule prompt-construction-variables/a1 -> :instruction "この間接がもたらす利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "This indirection decouples template prose from tool naming: renaming a tool requires changing one registry entry rather than editing every template.")
(defrule prompt-construction-providers -> :nucleus prompt-construction-providers/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-providers/a1 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-providers/a2)
(defrule prompt-construction-providers/n -> :instruction "提供元ごとの違いと、案内が無いときに起きる問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "Different LLM providers have meaningfully different capabilities and conventions: Anthropic models support tool_use content blocks and extended thinking, OpenAI models use function calling with structured output support, and inference providers like Fireworks have different context window limits.")
(defrule prompt-construction-providers/a1 -> :instruction "提供元ごとの案内の入れ方を 1 文で書く" :sample "The PromptComposer addresses this with mutually exclusive conditional sections gated on the model_provider field from the runtime environment context.")
(defrule prompt-construction-providers/a2 -> :instruction "提供元が不明のときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "Exactly one provider section (OpenAI, Anthropic, Fireworks) is included per prompt based on the active provider, and unknown providers receive no section (graceful degradation).")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching -> :nucleus prompt-construction-caching/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-caching/a1 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-caching/a2 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-caching/a3 :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-caching/a4)
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/n -> :instruction "入力の保存に対応する提供元への特別な分割を 1 文で書く" :sample "For providers that support input caching (currently Anthropic), the PromptComposer offers a compose_two_part() method that splits the assembled prompt into a stable part and a dynamic part.")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/a1 -> :instruction "節の印と、固定部分と変動部分への振り分けを 1 文で書く" :sample "Each section is annotated with a cacheable flag (defaulting to True); sections marked cacheable (base instructions, tool descriptions, safety policy) are concatenated into the stable part, and the remainder (environment metadata, session-specific context) into the dynamic part.")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/a2 -> :instruction "提供元に渡す形を 1 文で書く" :sample "The AnthropicAdapter structures these as a two-element content array: the stable block carries a cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"} header, while the dynamic block carries none.")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/a3 -> :instruction "保存の効果の見積もりを 1 文で書く" :sample "Since the system prompt is re-sent on every LLM call and the stable portion typically comprises 80–90% of the total, caching it yields substantial cost savings over a multi-turn session (approximately 88% reduction in input token cost for the cached portion).")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/a4 -> :instruction "対応しない提供元の扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "Providers that do not support this mechanism receive the full concatenated prompt as a single string, with no behavioral difference.")
(defrule prompt-construction-fallback -> :nucleus prompt-construction-fallback/n :elaboration-additional prompt-construction-fallback/a1 :purpose prompt-construction-fallback/a2)
(defrule prompt-construction-fallback/n -> :instruction "節のファイルが欠けたときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "If an individual section file is missing, the composer skips it and proceeds, so the agent starts with a slightly reduced prompt rather than failing.")
(defrule prompt-construction-fallback/a1 -> :instruction "組み立て全体が失敗したときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "If modular composition fails wholesale (e.g., the templates directory is absent), the builder falls back to a monolithic core template.")
(defrule prompt-construction-fallback/a2 -> :instruction "この二段の保険の目的を 1 文で書く" :sample "This guarantees agent startup under partial-deployment conditions.")
